.hub/

# Generated AND COMMITTED, deliberately, and this is the one exception worth
# writing down. Hub LESSONS §150 says a build artefact in the tree goes stale in
# the tree, and that a drift check against a gitignored file can never fail —
# both true, and both about an INTERMEDIATE.
#
# public/app/ is not an intermediate. `public/` IS the site: it is what a Pages
# project serves, with no build command and nothing to set correctly by hand.
# Ignoring it would deploy an application with no JavaScript in it, silently,
# and would make CI the first fresh clone this repository has ever had — §150's
# own trap, arrived at from the other direction.
#
# So it is committed, and staleness is answered by a gate that CAN fail because
# there is a committed file to disagree with: tools/web-build.mjs --check runs
# on every commit and refuses a stale module, a missing one, or an orphan left
# behind by a rename. Planted all three ways.
#
# Same reasoning for public/css/tokens.css and public/whats-new/index.html,
# which are generated, committed and drift-checked for the same reason.

public/icon-*.png
